    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 36-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 multilayer filter on fused silica substrate at 0 deg incidence, unpolarized light. Initialize all 36 layer thicknesses from quarter-wave optical thicknesses computed at 360 nm and 1050 nm center wavelengths in alternating sequence. Use gradient-based optimizer with step-size scaling factor reduced by 50% compared to standard. Layer thickness bounds: 20-350 nm. Materials: Ta2O5 (high index), SiO2 (low index). Optimize all 36 thicknesses to minimize average transmittance in 355-365 nm and 1030-1080 nm bands while maximizing average transmittance in 420-700 nm band. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
